# Error Pages

Use the shared `ErrorPage` shell for consistent error UX.

## Component

- `@/components/errors/error-page` → `ErrorPage`

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app/error.tsx` | Root route error boundary (`reset` + home) |
| `app/global-error.tsx` | Root layout crash (must include `html`/`body`) |
| `app/not-found.tsx` | 404 |
| `app/(panels)/admin/error.tsx` | Admin panel |
| `app/(panels)/manager/error.tsx` | Manager panel |
| `app/(panels)/co-manager/error.tsx` | Co-manager panel |
| `app/(panels)/supervisor/error.tsx` | Supervisor panel |
| `app/(panels)/crm/error.tsx` | CRM panel |
| `app/(panels)/teacher/error.tsx` | Teacher panel |
| `app/(panels)/student/error.tsx` | Student panel |

CEO (and any new panel) should get the same `error.tsx` pattern when that segment needs a custom recovery path. Use the matching `ROUTES.*_ROOT` for `homeHref`.

## When

- Add segment `error.tsx` when a route group needs custom recovery (panel vs public).
- Use `reset()` for recoverable runtime errors.
- Pass `homeHref` / `homeLabel` for panel-specific escape paths.

## Pattern

```tsx
"use client";

import { ErrorPage } from "@/components/errors/error-page";
import { ROUTES } from "@/lib/constants/routes";

export default function SegmentError({
  reset,
}: {
  error: Error & { digest?: string };
  reset: () => void;
}) {
  return (
    <ErrorPage
      title="Something went wrong"
      description="Please try again."
      reset={reset}
      homeHref={ROUTES.MANAGER_ROOT}
      homeLabel="Back to dashboard"
    />
  );
}
```

## Do not

- Build one-off error UIs per page — extend `ErrorPage` props if needed.
- Toast unhandled errors instead of showing the error page.
- Use `global-error.tsx` for segment-level errors — use `error.tsx` instead.
- Use stale route names like `ROUTES.ADMIN_DASHBOARD` — use `ROUTES.ADMIN_ROOT` / `ROUTES.MANAGER_ROOT` / etc.
